{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>Rav lakh</b> — You began to recount His praises; \"rav\" is yours and greater than you to recount of Him. Another interpretation: your master, who is greater than you — Adam haRishon, through whom death was decreed upon all, and it is impossible for you to escape it. Another interpretation: rav lakh — many times you acted against Me. You said: \"Send, I pray, by the hand You will send.\" And: \"Why have You dealt ill?\" \"The flock and cattle.\" And: \"The rock.\" I cannot bear you any longer. Another interpretation: even in a small matter that you do improperly, it is rav lakh relative to your wisdom. Another interpretation: by this He knows that rav lakh — for I am your master, for many times you defeated Me, and now you cannot defeat Me. Another interpretation: rav lakh — you have a master, but I have no master who can release My oath; therefore you shall not enter. Another interpretation: the hour has arrived that you have a master, for the time of Joshua has already come, and his leadership cannot be recognized while you are alive. Another interpretation: rav lakh — do not fear the Angel of Death, for your master will attend to you. Another interpretation: rav lakh — many blessings are prepared for you: \"How abundant is Your goodness that You have hidden for those who fear You.\""], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The verse quoted at the end is Psalm 31:20. The midrashic citations of Moses' words reference several prior incidents; they carry no verse addresses in the source."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:08:44.891262423Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}